* NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design. Simulated results; models as stated; nothing has been built or measured.
* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
*
* wpf_models.lib — additions for the WP-F revision 0.3 check runs (hardware/aed-main/sim/rev3-wpf). Built by hand
* from datasheet figures; NOT makers' models. Used together with ../charger-storage/models/datasheet_models.lib
* (DEPMOS, SMF15CA, BAT54, BAV199, ZENER, TLP187, BSS138, J177), which is included by every netlist here.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* GP02-40 4 kV rectifier, gate-steering diode D1127..D1132 — RE-READ 2026-11-27:
*   [DS] Vishay doc 88635, revision 09-Aug-2022 ("Not for New Designs"): VRRM 4,000 V; IF(AV) 0.25 A;
*   VF <= 3.0 V at 1.0 A; IR <= 5.0 uA at VDC, 25 C; <= 50 uA at VDC, 100 C; trr typ 2.0 us; CJ typ 3.0 pF at
*   4 V; DO-41 (DO-204AL). Fig. 4 (typical): IR at 100 C ~1.3 uA at 5 % of VRRM rising to ~3 uA at 100 %;
*   at 25 C ~0.01-0.03 uA. So leakage is almost flat with voltage (a "saturation" current), and the
*   guaranteed maximum is ~17x the typical curve.
*   Model: junction for the forward path; reverse leakage as a current source cathode -> anode that is
*   flat above ~1 V of reverse bias: I = ilk * (1 - exp(-Vr/0.5 V)) (continued linearly through 0 V so its slope
*   has no kink - a kinked version made the transient solver diverge). ilk is a parameter:
*     ilk = 50u  "hot bound": the 100 C datasheet MAXIMUM applied at 70 C (pessimistic by ~8x for 30 K of
*                margin and ~17x max/typ) [EST, deliberately bounding]
*     ilk = 5u   25 C datasheet maximum
*     ilk = 0.5u cold [EST]
.subckt GPL a k params: ilk=5u
D1 a k DGPL
.model DGPL d(is=1e-10 n=3.2 rs=1 cjo=3p tt=2u)
BLK k a I = {ilk}*(v(k,a) > 0 ? 1-exp(-v(k,a)/0.5) : v(k,a)/0.5)
.ends GPL

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* IXTT2N170D2 temperature factors — RE-READ 2026-11-27, IXYS DS100418B(02/12) Fig. 12 "Normalized Breakdown and
* Threshold Voltages vs. Junction Temperature" (curve readings, typical):
*   |VGS(off)| normalised: 0.85 at -40 C, ~0.89 at -20 C, 1.00 at 25 C, ~1.06 at 50 C, ~1.11 at 70 C
*   BVDSX (VGS -5 V) normalised: ~0.985 at -40 C, ~0.98 at -20..0 C, 1.00 at 25 C, rising above
* charger-storage assumed 0.93 / 1.06 for VGS(off) and 0.94 for BVDSX (from the 10N100D2's Fig. 11).
* Ratings used here: 1,666 V at -20 C (0.98 x 1,700), 1,700 V at 25-70 C (VDSX is specified 25-150 C).
* Off-state leakage (rleak = VDSX / I): datasheet maxima 25 uA at 25 C, 500 uA at 125 C; log-interpolated
* (as charger-storage) 70 C 96 uA -> 17.7 Mohm, -20 C 6.5 uA -> 262 Mohm [EST]. Device itself: DEPMOS with
* the 2N170D2 set (kp 0.6, rd 6.0, Cgs 3.57 nF, Cgd0 485 pF, Cds0 760 pF) from datasheet_models.lib.
